+// On the staff code step (/admin/login.php, after the right staff ID and password), the person can ask for help: their
+// name and a phone or another email to reach them. It becomes an owners' Pulse case (Security, key staffmail:<id>, one
+// case per request). The form isn't signed in, so the case shows first who the login is, its work email now, its last
+// sign-in and the contact given, marked not verified; each button asks "Have you confirmed this is them?" first:
+//   Change work email          StaffLogin::setEmail; the old address is told
+//   Reset the mailbox password CPanelMail::setPassword (our own work domain only); shown once to the owner
+//   New setup link             StaffLogin::reset (their sessions end, password and authenticator cleared); the link is
+//                              shown to the owner to hand over, never only emailed to the mailbox they can't reach
+// Every action goes in the staff log (StaffLogin::log) and on the case (Pulse notes). Owners only.
+// Requests are held in staff_mail_requests (class "never" in staging-tables.php: sign-in recovery, empty on staging).
+declare(strict_types=1);
+
+require_once __DIR__ . '/StaffLogin.php';
